MINT0/MINT1 grids for the MINT2-only tests (vfold/myLaunch.sh -o).

'output <procdir> --vfold-with-tests' runs madvfold/test/setupVfoldTests.sh,
which copies <proc>/ from this directory (if it exists) into
vfold/test/grids of the generated process directory, together with this
README. <proc> is the name of the process used by MadGraph for its
SubProcesses/P0_<proc> directory, whatever the name of the process
directory and the order of the particles in the generate command (e.g.
epem_bbbxbx for 'generate e+ e- > b b~ b b~ [QCD]', also in
madvfold/DEV/eebbbb_vfgen; the grids are installed only for processes
with a single P directory).

MadGraph7: the grids are those of mg5amcnlo (branch vfold5381cg) at the same
step, with their mint_grids converted by madvfold/test/convertGrids381to7.py
(step 14e part 4/4: nintegrals is 26=6+2*10 in MG5aMC 3.8.1 and 38=6+2*16 in
MadGraph7, whose read_grids_from_file stops on the old ones with 'Bad real
number').

Each <proc>/folding_<f1>_<f2>_<f3>[_Delta] directory holds, for one
folding without/with MC@NLO-Delta, only what myLaunch.sh -o uses:
- job_status.pkl: the list of integration jobs (in -o mode MG5 keeps only
  the jobs with a res_1.dat, rereads their results from it, and takes the
  folding from the run_card)
- aS.txt: the aS(MZ) of the grids, which myLaunch.sh sets in the
  param_card for MINT2
- <Pdir>/GF<channel>: the grids of the GF channels used in the tests
  (res_1.dat, mint_grids, res_1, grid.MC_integer and results.dat)

epem_bbbxbx (eebbbb, channel GF11.0):
- folding_8_4_1 and folding_1_1_1 come from vfold5363 (MG5 3.6.3), which
  took aS(MZ)=0.119 from the PDF set even with lpp=0
- folding_8_4_1_Delta and folding_1_1_1_Delta come from Delta physics
  runs in vfold5381 (MG5 3.8.1, aS(MZ)=0.118), as the MINT1 upper envelope
  must be computed with Delta

epem_bbxmummupg (eemumubbg, channel GF11.0):
- folding_8_4_1 and folding_1_1_1 come from the default physics runs of
  GEN_proc.sh in vfold5381 (MG5 3.8.1, aS(MZ)=0.118), Events/run_gen841
  and Events/run_gen111 of eemumubbg_vfalt (branch vfold5381cgOldGrids)
- the job_status.pkl of run_gen111 was not saved: that of folding_1_1_1
  was built from that of run_gen841, with fold_string '1 1 1' and the
  results of each channel from its res_1.dat in run_gen111 (checked in
  eebbbb: the f111 -o events are the same with the original job_status.pkl
  and with one built from the f841 one)
- there are no Delta grids yet: -o with ENV_MCATNLODELTA=1 fails
